{"agent":"fix-review-triage-flags","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The guard detects \"flag was given\" by truthiness: `for flag, given in (... (\"--finding\", a.finding), ... (\"--probe\", a.probe)) if given`. Any falsy-but-explicit flag value therefore bypasses the refusal and falls through to the full review path. Concretely, `ddflow review ITEM --finding 0` sets `a.finding == 0`, which is falsy, so `stray` stays empty and the code proceeds past the guard (past `if len(ids) > 1`) into the normal review, starting exactly the 25-minute reviewer run that bug B3531d304ec is supposed to prevent. The same happens with `ddflow review ITEM --probe \"\"` (empty-string probe), where `a.probe == \"\"` is falsy and the reviewer is contacted. The stated contract (\"`--finding`/`--refuted`/`--confirmed`/`--probe` on a plain `review` are refused (exit 1) before any reviewer is contacted\") is violated for these inputs; flag-presence should be tested against the argparse default (`is not None`, or comparing the parsed value to the default), not against truthiness.","digest":"2b2b28d0b6e2688d","location":"ddflow/surfaces/commands/review.py (the `stray` guard, ~line 55)","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/surfaces/commands/review.py (the `stray` guard, ~line 55)"}],"chunks_total":2,"coverage":"2/2 chunk(s) reviewed","diff_chars":7879,"diff_sha":"54d8f849cf8c1908b2827641f290375fd8f3d13e8147bbbde7dfd2a6652ef19d","diff_source":"main..HEAD + working tree in /home/delian/src/.ddflow-worktrees/B-fix-review-triage-flags","elapsed_s":131.4,"family":"deepseek","findings":1,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","reason":"","reviewed":[1,2],"reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewer_digest":"d34b8af1b4a590b5","status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/surfaces/commands/review.py (the `stray` guard, ~line 55)"],"unreviewed":[]},"gate":"rubber_duck","reason":"1 finding(s)"},"id":"eec6d219381717f417d869